From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:30:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6afe: complete the hw vote on an error response

The ADSP answers a failed LPASS core hw vote with a basic response that
q6afe_callback() does not handle, so the vote waits the full 3 s timeout
with afe->lock held. The vote response handler also reads a status
field past its 4 byte payload.

A basic response with an error status for the vote now completes the
wait with that status; success still comes with the vote response. The
vote response sets the handle and a status of 0 when its payload holds
the handle, and ADSP_EBADPARAM when it is shorter, so the vote fails at
once.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
index d7e5e4c70..7fe42f3bf 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
@@ -996,6 +996,13 @@ static int q6afe_callback(struct apr_device *adev, const struct apr_resp_pkt *da
 				wake_up(&afe->wait);
 			}
 			break;
+		case AFE_CMD_REMOTE_LPASS_CORE_HW_VOTE_REQUEST:
+			if (res->status) {
+				afe->result.opcode = AFE_CMD_RSP_REMOTE_LPASS_CORE_HW_VOTE_REQUEST;
+				afe->result.status = res->status;
+				wake_up(&afe->wait);
+			}
+			break;
 		case AFE_CMD_REMOTE_LPASS_CORE_HW_DEVOTE_REQUEST:
 			break;
 		default:
@@ -1005,9 +1012,13 @@ static int q6afe_callback(struct apr_device *adev, const struct apr_resp_pkt *da
 	}
 		break;
 	case AFE_CMD_RSP_REMOTE_LPASS_CORE_HW_VOTE_REQUEST:
-		afe->hw_vote_handle = *(const uint32_t *)data->payload;
 		afe->result.opcode = hdr->opcode;
-		afe->result.status = res->status;
+		if (data->payload_size < sizeof(afe->hw_vote_handle)) {
+			afe->result.status = ADSP_EBADPARAM;
+		} else {
+			afe->hw_vote_handle = *(const uint32_t *)data->payload;
+			afe->result.status = 0;
+		}
 		wake_up(&afe->wait);
 		break;
 	default:
